                <pb facs="0544" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg522"/>

                <head>No. 54.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Earl Granville to Sir E.
                    Thornton.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-05-17"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 17,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[From British Blue Book “North America,” No. 9, (1872,) p.
                    21.]</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your dispatch of the 30th
                    ultimo, reporting your conversation with Mr. Fish on the subject of the indirect
                    claims; and, in reply, I have to acquaint you that Her Majesty’s Government
                    approve’ your guarded language on this subject, as reported in your
                    dispatch.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GRANVILLE.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
